<title>ITALY: Montedison unit wins $180 mln Brazil deal.</title>
<headline>Montedison unit wins $180 mln Brazil deal.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Tecnimont, the engineering arm of Montedison, said on Wednesday that it had won a contract worth $180 million for the construction of a petrochemical plant at Triunfo in Brazil.</p>
<p>Tecnimont won the contract from Ipiranga Petroquimica, consisting of Ipiranga and Hoechst Brazil, to build the plant to produce polypropylene and polyethylene. The plant is scheduled to be completed by the second half of 1999.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
